# DS605 Lab 8 — Decision Trees & Support Vector Machines from Scratch

UCI **Banknote Authentication** dataset (1,372 samples, 4 features, genuine vs forged).
Decision Tree and Linear SVM are implemented **from scratch with NumPy/Pandas**, compared with scikit-learn, extended with kernel SVMs, and benchmarked together on all four features.

## Repository contents
| Path | Description |
|---|---|
| `DS605_Lab8_Decision_Tree_SVM.ipynb` | Full runnable notebook (Parts A–D), executed with outputs included |
| `data_banknote_authentication.txt` | Dataset |
| `plots/` | All decision-boundary, margin, tree and comparison figures |
| `results/` | CSV tables: depth/criterion study, `C` / learning-rate / iteration studies, kernel comparison, final comparison |

Run it: `pip install -r requirements.txt` then `jupyter notebook DS605_Lab8_Decision_Tree_SVM.ipynb` (Run All). Everything uses `random_state = 42`.

## What was implemented
- **Decision tree (`DecisionTreeScratch`)** — Gini and entropy, vectorised threshold search (midpoints of sorted values, cumulative class counts), recursive growth, stopping rules (pure node, `max_depth`, `min_samples_split`, `min_samples_leaf`, minimum gain), prediction, rule export and a drawn tree.
- **Linear soft-margin SVM (`LinearSVMScratch`)** — labels mapped to ±1, features scaled with training-set statistics, hinge loss + L2, full-batch sub-gradient descent, learning-rate decay. Objective is normalised so `C` has the same meaning as in scikit-learn.
- **Own helpers (no sklearn):** stratified train/test split, standard scaler, stratified k-fold, accuracy/precision/recall/F1 (cross-checked against scikit-learn).
- scikit-learn is used only for comparison models, `make_moons`/`make_circles`, and a grid search for the RBF SVM.
- One stratified 80/20 split (1,098 train / 274 test) is reused by every model. 2-D plots use `variance` + `skewness`; final metrics use all four features.

